{"c":[{"id":"166b843e5f81c9fe","sum":"B15: a stop or takeOver revokes the act grant at once (a write in flight is refused; fakes refuse ungranted acts only with enforceGrants); Chrome builds its web AX tree seconds after the reader asks, so wait for the form's fields before acting.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T124042Z-0ff3662999b3099a","text":"A stop or takeOver revokes the task's act grant at once, so a write still on its way is refused and the run ends as stopped by you; test fakes (FakeApp, SocketReader) refuse acts without a grant only when enforceGrants is set.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T124042Z-b3569a4cf63d6bee","text":"Chrome builds its web AX tree seconds after the reader asks for it: wait until the form's fields are in the screen model before acting, or the first plans stop with target-not-found (B15 explore run).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ead499ab30c4256f","sum":"B15: caret-screen acts only under a helper actGrant (task, pid, window; 120 s, monotonic; --act-pids for fixtures; only accepted offers get one). Chrome takes AXValue on web inputs but ignores AXSelectedText; background WKWebView drops writes; the walk check caught each.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T124106Z-598a6c678d777d69","text":"caret-screen acts only under a helper actGrant (task, pid, window; 120 s max, monotonic); --act-pids is for fixture tests. Only accepted offers get grants (Executor.run opts.grant); a consumer runPlan never does, so the product refuses it (B15).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T124106Z-77698db11d4c9d42","text":"Real targets (B15): Chrome takes AXValue on web inputs, front or back, but answers AXSelectedText ok and changes nothing; WKWebView in background-only caret-fixture drops value and insert silently; TextEdit takes all. The executor's walk check caught each drop.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
